From 48a56b23a7d7bd0cf9b08f87655db9d817a71fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:46:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(examples): pin the catalog refusal.txt files to LF

The refusal test of example_catalog compares the refusal lines byte for
byte. No rule in .gitattributes covered refusal.txt, so a checkout with
core.autocrlf=true wrote CRLF and two tests failed on Windows.

Fixes #3628

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitattributes | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
index 5afdc9796..1f2d7997b 100644
--- a/.gitattributes
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ testdata/**/*.obj text eol=lf
 docs/tester-kits/**/*.nc text eol=lf
 # Shipped example programs, including the catalog, are pinned byte for byte.
 examples/**/*.nc text eol=lf
+# The catalog refusal goldens are compared byte for byte by example_catalog.
+examples/catalog/**/refusal.txt text eol=lf
 
 # Shell scripts run on macOS / Linux: a CR would break the shebang.
 *.sh text eol=lf
